# cpu_alu.checks - one row per CHECK of fixtures/src/cpu_alu.s (D-125, plan 03-12). Columns separated by one TAB: check index (1-based, the entry number of the DCK1 table), slug, class tag, meaning.
# Class tags: MAN:<page> (the literal is a manual page value; the page label must be in fixtures/lib/cites.txt), GUEST:<model> (the expected byte is computed in the guest, the table entry is an XOR mask of $00),
# ASSUMED:<LED-id> (the literal is DuoSpool's own model, an assumption: decimal N, Z and C, the decimal borrow value, T mode with decimal mode, the Z of TSB and TRB and the stored result of TRB; the entry is written in a later plan).
# A GUEST row aggregates 32 sums or shifts and expects a difference byte of zero. P read through PHP then PLA is masked with $C3 (N V Z C) or $83 (N Z C) or a single bit: B, I and T are not part of the literal.
# A pass is not a support claim (ER-4).
id=4
checks=96
1	and-imm	MAN:S8-18	AND immediate: A = $F0 AND $3C gives $30
2	ora-imm	MAN:S8-58	ORA immediate: A = $30 OR $0C gives $3C
3	eor-imm	MAN:S8-47	EOR immediate: A = $FF EOR $0F gives $F0
4	and-flag-n	MAN:S8-18	AND sets N from the result and leaves V and C alone: V and C set by PLP, $FF AND $80 gives N, so the P byte masked with $C3 is $C1
5	and-flag-z	MAN:S8-18	AND sets Z from the result and leaves V and C alone: $0F AND $F0 gives zero, so the P byte masked with $C3 is $43 (V, Z, C)
6	ora-flag-n	MAN:S8-58	ORA sets N from the result and leaves V and C alone: $00 OR $80, V and C set, masked P byte $C1
7	eor-flag-z	MAN:S8-47	EOR sets Z from the result and leaves V and C alone: $80 EOR $80 gives zero, V and C set, masked P byte $43
8	and-zp	MAN:S8-18	AND zero page: $0F AND the cell $2010 ($01) gives $01
9	ora-indy	MAN:S8-58	ORA (zz),Y: $20 OR the byte at $2603 ($05) gives $25 (Y = 3)
10	eor-absx	MAN:S8-47	EOR absolute,X: $FF EOR the byte at $2502 ($07) gives $F8 (X = 2)
11	adc-imm	MAN:S8-17	ADC immediate with C clear: $10 + $20 gives $30
12	adc-carry-in	MAN:S8-17	ADC adds the carry: $10 + $20 + C = $31
13	adc-carry-out	MAN:S8-17	ADC sets C and Z for $FF + $01 = $100: masked P byte $03 (N and V clear)
14	adc-overflow-pos	MAN:S8-17	ADC sets V and N for $7F + $01 = $80 (two positives give a negative): masked P byte $C0
15	adc-overflow-neg	MAN:S8-17	ADC of $80 + $80 = $100 sets V, Z and C (two negatives give a positive): masked P byte $43
16	adc-model-result	GUEST:adc-binary	ADC against the in-guest bit-serial adder over 16 edge pairs with C clear and set: the OR of every result difference is zero
17	adc-model-flags	GUEST:adc-binary	ADC N V Z C against the in-guest adder over the same 32 sums: the OR of every flag difference is zero
18	adc-zp	MAN:S8-17	ADC zero page with C set: $10 + the cell value $01 + 1 gives $12
19	adc-zpx	MAN:S8-17	ADC zero page,X (X = 3) with C set: $10 + the cell value $02 + 1 gives $13
20	adc-indx	MAN:S8-17	ADC (zz,X) (X = 4) with C set: $10 + the cell value $04 + 1 gives $15
21	adc-abs	MAN:S8-17	ADC absolute with C set: $10 + the cell value $06 + 1 gives $17
22	adc-absx	MAN:S8-17	ADC absolute,X (X = 2) with C set: $10 + the cell value $07 + 1 gives $18
23	adc-absy	MAN:S8-17	ADC absolute,Y (Y = 5) with C set: $10 + the cell value $08 + 1 gives $19
24	sbc-imm	MAN:S8-74	SBC immediate with C set (no borrow): $50 - $20 - 0 = $30
25	sbc-borrow-in	MAN:S8-74	SBC subtracts the complement of C (A - M - not C): C clear gives $50 - $20 - 1 = $2F
26	sbc-borrow-out	MAN:S8-74	SBC of $20 - $30 with C set borrows: A = $F0, so C is clear and N is set: masked P byte $80
27	sbc-overflow	MAN:S8-74	SBC sets V for $80 - $01 = $7F (a negative minus a positive gives a positive): C stays set, masked P byte $41
28	sbc-model-result	GUEST:sbc-binary	SBC against the in-guest adder fed the complement of M (A + not M + C, S8-74) over 16 edge pairs with C clear and set: the OR of every result difference is zero
29	sbc-model-flags	GUEST:sbc-binary	SBC N V Z C against the in-guest adder over the same 32 differences: the OR of every flag difference is zero
30	dec-adc-simple	MAN:S8-17	ADC in decimal mode on valid BCD, C clear: $12 + $34 gives $46
31	dec-adc-wrap-value	MAN:S8-17	ADC in decimal mode on $99 + $01 leaves the decimal sum $00 in A
32	dec-adc-wrap-c	ASSUMED:LED-CPU-0010	ADC in decimal mode on $99 + $01: C set from the decimal carry (the page lists C without defining it in decimal mode, D-99)
33	dec-adc-wrap-z	ASSUMED:LED-CPU-0010	ADC in decimal mode on $99 + $01: Z set from the adjusted result $00 (D-99)
34	dec-adc-v-kept-set	MAN:S8-17	ADC in decimal mode leaves V alone: V set by PLP before SED, $01 + $01, V still set (binary mode would clear it): masked V bit $40
35	dec-sbc-simple	MAN:S8-74	SBC in decimal mode on valid BCD, C set: $46 - $12 gives $34
36	dec-sbc-digit-borrow	MAN:S8-74	SBC in decimal mode borrows from the high digit: $40 - $01 gives $39
37	dec-sbc-borrow-in	MAN:S8-74	SBC in decimal mode subtracts the complement of C: C clear, $46 - $12 - 1 gives $33
38	dec-sbc-borrow-value	ASSUMED:LED-CPU-0010	SBC in decimal mode on $12 - $34 (a borrow out): A = $78, the ten's complement of the difference (the project's reading of a decimal borrow, D-99)
39	dec-sbc-borrow-c	ASSUMED:LED-CPU-0010	SBC in decimal mode on $12 - $34: C clear for the borrow (D-99)
40	dec-sbc-v-kept	MAN:S8-74	SBC in decimal mode leaves V alone: V clear, $80 - $01 (binary mode would set it): masked V bit $00
41	t-adc-cell	MAN:S8-17	SET then ADC: the sum goes to the zero-page cell $20F0 (X = $F0): $10 + $20 = $30 in the cell
42	t-adc-a-kept	MAN:S8-17	SET then ADC leaves A alone: A stays $77
43	t-adc-flags	MAN:S8-17	SET then ADC takes its flags from the cell sum: cell $FF + $01 = $00 sets Z and C (A = $00 would give neither): masked P byte $03
44	t-and	MAN:S8-18	SET then AND: the cell $F0 AND $3C = $30 is stored in the cell
45	t-ora	MAN:S8-58	SET then ORA: the cell $30 OR $0C = $3C is stored in the cell
46	t-eor	MAN:S8-47	SET then EOR: the cell $FF EOR $0F = $F0 is stored in the cell
47	t-cleared-next	MAN:S8-17	T mode applies only to the instruction right after SET: SET, CLC, then ADC works on A ($41 + $01 = $42)
48	t-decimal	ASSUMED:LED-CPU-0010	SED before SET, then ADC: the cell $19 + $01 = $20 in decimal (the combination of T mode and decimal mode is stated on no page, D-99)
49	asl-model-result	GUEST:shift	ASL A against the in-guest bit-serial shifter over 16 edge values with C clear and set: the OR of every result difference is zero
50	asl-model-flags	GUEST:shift	ASL A N Z C against the in-guest shifter over the same 32 inputs (C is the bit shifted out, not the old C): the OR of every flag difference is zero
51	asl-mem-zp	MAN:S8-19	ASL zero page is a read-modify-write: the cell $2050 ($81) becomes $02
52	lsr-model-result	GUEST:shift	LSR A against the in-guest shifter over 16 edge values with C clear and set: the OR of every result difference is zero
53	lsr-model-flags	GUEST:shift	LSR A N Z C against the in-guest shifter over the same 32 inputs: the OR of every flag difference is zero
54	lsr-n-clear	MAN:S8-56	LSR always clears N (bit 7 is filled with zero): $FF loads with N set, LSR gives $7F, masked P byte $01 (C only)
55	lsr-mem-abs	MAN:S8-56	LSR absolute: the cell $2700 ($03) becomes $01
56	rol-model-result	GUEST:shift	ROL A against the in-guest shifter (C comes in at bit 0) over 16 edge values with C clear and set: the OR of every result difference is zero
57	rol-model-flags	GUEST:shift	ROL A N Z C against the in-guest shifter over the same 32 inputs: the OR of every flag difference is zero
58	rol-carry-in	MAN:S8-68	ROL rotates C into bit 0: C set, $40 gives $81
59	rol-mem-zpx	MAN:S8-68	ROL zero page,X rotates C in: C set, the cell $2053 ($C0) becomes $81 (X = 3)
60	ror-model-result	GUEST:shift	ROR A against the in-guest shifter (C comes in at bit 7) over 16 edge values with C clear and set: the OR of every result difference is zero
61	ror-model-flags	GUEST:shift	ROR A N Z C against the in-guest shifter over the same 32 inputs: the OR of every flag difference is zero
62	ror-carry-in	MAN:S8-69	ROR rotates C into bit 7: C set, $02 gives $81
63	ror-mem-absx	MAN:S8-69	ROR absolute,X rotates C in: C set, the cell $2702 ($02) becomes $81 (X = 2)
64	inc-a	MAN:S8-48	INC accumulator: $41 becomes $42
65	inc-a-wrap	MAN:S8-48	INC accumulator wraps $FF to $00: Z set, C untouched (set by PLP), masked P byte $03
66	dec-a	MAN:S8-44	DEC accumulator: $42 becomes $41
67	dec-a-wrap	MAN:S8-44	DEC accumulator wraps $00 to $FF: N set, C untouched (set by PLP), masked P byte $81
68	inc-mem-zp	MAN:S8-48	INC zero page: the cell $2050 ($7F) becomes $80
69	dec-mem-absx	MAN:S8-44	DEC absolute,X: the cell $2702 ($01) becomes $00 (X = 2)
70	inx-value	MAN:S8-49	INX: $7E becomes $7F (read back with TXA)
71	iny-value	MAN:S8-50	INY: $10 becomes $11 (read back with TYA)
72	iny-wrap	MAN:S8-50	INY wraps $FF to $00: Z set, C untouched, masked P byte $03
73	dex-value	MAN:S8-45	DEX: $80 becomes $7F (read back with TXA; the page's function line prints Y, its title, opcode CA and mnemonic are X)
74	dex-wrap	MAN:S8-45	DEX wraps $00 to $FF: N set, C untouched, masked P byte $81
75	dey-value	MAN:S8-46	DEY: $01 becomes $00 (read back with TYA)
76	cmp-gt	MAN:S8-41	CMP of $30 with $20 (A - M, S8-41): C set, Z and N clear, V untouched (set by PLP): masked P byte $41
77	cmp-eq	MAN:S8-41	CMP of equal bytes sets Z and C, V untouched: masked P byte $43
78	cmp-lt	MAN:S8-41	CMP of $10 with $20 clears C (C was set) and sets N from the difference $F0, V untouched: masked P byte $C0
79	cmp-zpx	MAN:S8-41	CMP zero page,X with equal bytes ($02 and the cell $2013) sets Z and C (X = 3): masked P byte $03
80	cpx-gt	MAN:S8-42	CPX of $30 with $20 sets C: masked P byte $01
81	cpx-lt	MAN:S8-42	CPX of $10 with $20 clears C (C was set) and sets N: masked P byte $80
82	cpx-abs	MAN:S8-42	CPX absolute with X = $06 against the byte $06 at $2500 sets Z and C: masked P byte $03
83	cpy-lt	MAN:S8-43	CPY of $10 with $20 clears C (C was set) and sets N: masked P byte $80
84	cpy-zp	MAN:S8-43	CPY zero page with Y = $01 against the cell $2010 ($01) sets Z and C: masked P byte $03
85	bit-imm	MAN:S8-25	BIT immediate: $01 AND $C0 is zero (Z set) and N and V come from the operand bits 7 and 6 (the flag row of the page reads M7 and M6): masked P byte $C2
86	bit-zp	MAN:S8-25	BIT zero page: A = $0F with the cell $2050 = $40: Z set, N clear, V set from bit 6: masked P byte $42
87	bit-absx	MAN:S8-25	BIT absolute,X: A = $FF with the cell $2702 = $80: Z clear, N set, V clear: masked P byte $80 (X = 2)
88	tsb-zp-mem	MAN:S8-103	TSB zero page stores A OR M: A = $0F, the cell $2050 ($30) becomes $3F
89	tsb-abs-mem	MAN:S8-103	TSB absolute stores A OR M: A = $81, the cell $2700 ($02) becomes $83
90	tsb-z-set	ASSUMED:LED-CPU-0010	TSB: Z is set when A AND the old memory byte is zero (A = $0F, cell $F0). The page lists Z without saying where it comes from; N and V of TSB are not asserted (S8-103 against pcetech)
91	tsb-z-clear	ASSUMED:LED-CPU-0010	TSB: Z is clear when A AND the old memory byte is not zero (A = $01, cell $FF)
92	trb-zp-mem	ASSUMED:LED-CPU-0010	TRB zero page clears the bits of A in memory (the page formula M <- not A AND M; its prose says the result is not stored, so the stored result is the project's reading): A = $0F, the cell $2050 ($FF) becomes $F0
93	trb-z-set	ASSUMED:LED-CPU-0010	TRB: Z is set when A AND the old memory byte is zero (A = $0F, cell $F0); N and V of TRB are not asserted
94	tst-zp	MAN:S8-104	TST #imm,zero page: $01 AND the cell $2050 ($FE) is zero (Z set); N and V come from the memory byte bits 7 and 6: masked P byte $C2
95	tst-zpx	MAN:S8-104	TST #imm,zero page,X: $80 AND the cell $2053 ($80) is not zero; N set, V clear: masked P byte $80 (X = 3)
96	tst-absx	MAN:S8-104	TST #imm,absolute,X: $FF AND the cell $2702 ($40) is not zero; V set from bit 6, N clear: masked P byte $40 (X = 2)
